{"attachments":[{"content_type":null,"filename":"Solomon.jpg","id":"746602356644380672","local_path":"discord/roanoke-season-3/attachments/733826617524224050/746602356644380672-Solomon.jpg","message_id":"746602356787118135","sha256":"099d662f050ebb80061c06c0302eb388f870cf17f7dcada2ae723282a669164d","size":23441,"url":"https://cdn.discordapp.com/attachments/733826617524224050/746602356644380672/Solomon.jpg?ex=6abfea61&is=6abe98e1&hm=33daac865c275864c5b8e437a232ef43d5c4b05e6d3bc272e0ead2f17bef3f86&"}],"author":{"display_name":"Orxta","id":"343605682580488215","is_bot":0,"username":"robdor."},"author_id":"343605682580488215","channel_id":"733826617524224050","content":"Solomon flies straight toward the creature emerging from the hunger. Arcane words ring in the air as he casts power word stun on the abomination. The creatures instantly ceases all movement. Solomon leaps off his flying mount and lands on the head of the creature. He turns to the combatants and cries,\n\n“I will tear the power from this creature and ascend to the heavens! Behold the birth of a god!”\n\nNo sooner does he finish his short monologue than a pair of black portals appear above Croatoan as its chains begin to glow with hellfire. Inky black tentacles grab Solomon and slam him to the ground. It was a ruse! It is not affected by the power word stun spell. It whips him around and slams him into the ground. Solomon lays in the mud in a bloody heap, unmoving. The creature turns his attention away from the pitiful form on the ground to more succulent prey.","created_at":"2020-08-22T05:31:13.059000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"746602356787118135","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
